Lab 7: Deploy VM Templates
Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Create reusable VM templates with predefined configurations using OpenShift Virtualization
Deploy multiple virtual machines efficiently using parameterized templates
Write validation and monitoring scripts to verify VM deployment consistency and performance
Understand template-based deployment best practices for standard, storage-backed, and database workloads
Troubleshoot common template deployment and networking issues
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic understanding of Kubernetes concepts (pods, services, namespaces)
Familiarity with YAML configuration files and bash scripting
Knowledge of Linux command line operations
Understanding of virtualization concepts (CPU, memory, disks, networking)
Completion of previous OpenShift Virtualization labs or equivalent experience
Required Knowledge Areas
OpenShift CLI (oc) commands
Virtual machine lifecycle management
Resource allocation and management
Basic networking concepts in virtualized environments
Basic bash scripting (loops, functions, conditionals)
