Start all five VMs and wait for them to come up:

for vm in basic-vm-01 basic-vm-02 basic-vm-03 advanced-vm-01 postgres-vm-01; do
  oc patch vm $vm -n vm-templates --type merge -p '{"spec":{"running":true}}'
done

# Poll status until all VMs report Running (Ctrl+C once all show Running)
watch oc get vms -n vm-templates
Deliverable for Task 2: oc get vms -n vm-templates shows five VMs (basic-vm-01, basic-vm-02, basic-vm-03, advanced-vm-01, postgres-vm-01), each with STATUS equal to Running. oc get pvc -n vm-templates shows three bound PVCs: advanced-vm-01-disk, postgres-vm-01-db-disk, and postgres-vm-01-log-disk.

